    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0237" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/814.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                            Germany to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-21T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 21, 1912—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>German minister at Peking instructed to join colleagues of four-power group in
                    protesting against Belgian loan, in which, according to information received by
                    German Foreign Office, both English and French bankers are interested. Germany
                    considers that it would be very unwise to increase size of group, which has
                    already been made somewhat unwieldy by the admission of Japanese syndicate and
                    Russia, whose entry was agreed to for political rather than financial
                    reasons.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leishman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
